      },
      {
        "budget_share": 0.30,
        "family": "pipelined_m",
        "ranges": [
          {"choices": [], "high": 18, "low": 16, "param": "data_width"},
          {"choices": [], "high": 20, "low": 14, "param": "n_iter"},
          {"choices": [], "high": 4, "low": -2, "param": "angle_guard"},
          {"choices": [], "high": 2, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"},
          {"choices": ["round", "trunc"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding"},
          {"choices": [], "high": 3, "low": 2, "param": "m"}
        ],
        "why": "protect / push the selection corner (min power_index, currently 2.38 at W=16,N=16), and test whether m=3 keeps throughput >= 50 while cutting FF/power"
      }
    ],
    "rationale": "The feasible front is owned entirely by pipelined_m (best power_index 2.38 vs pipelined's 3.86, and pipelined_m reaches 19.23 accuracy bits vs pipelined's 15.56), so concentrate here. Two gaps are visible: (1) n_iter was only sampled 15..19 although the registry allows 4..30, and for pipelined_m throughput = Fmax essentially independent of N, so the accuracy tail is artificially cut — the reported HV 181.2 is dominated by the single term (40 - 3.8)*(16.9 - 12) = 177.4, i.e. by the highest-accuracy front point, so raising a_max is the cheapest HV gain; (2) data_width was only sampled to 23, but throughput is 56.1 MSPS at W=23 (57 at W=22), leaving ~1-2 widths of room before the 50 MSPS floor. Widening n_iter to 30 at data_width ~22-24 should move a_max from 16.9 toward the 19+ bits already observed, while a smaller slice checks the low-power corner and m=3. pipelined (best throughput 163 but best feasible power 3.86, accuracy 15.56) stays off the search this round; it is dominated on both objectives that matter for selection."
  }
, "rationale": "mapper: widen_niter_datawidth_for_pipelined_m (feasible front is pipelined_m-only; accuracy tail truncated)"}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Budget is exhausted (200/200 evals) and this is the final round, so only stop/infeasible are valid. Infeasible is ruled out: 110 of 200 evaluations are feasible, and the selection rule (min power_index) is already satisfiable — the front's cheapest point, pipelined_m [W=16 N=16 angle_guard=2 frac_guard=1 round m=2], has power_index=2.38 with throughput 78.8 MSPS (>=50) and max_abs_err 1.77e-4 (<=2.44e-4), i.e. it meets both constraints. The front is also well-covered for the hypervolume objective: power_index spans 2.38..5.04 and accuracy_bits spans 12.5..20 (HV reference 12), with 26 Pareto designs and a +61.5% HV gain this round, so further mapping is not warranted. Both families on the front (pipelined, pipelined_m) were explored, and the registry has no unexplored family left to add. Stopping on the current front."
  ,
  "next_plan": null
}
